# Build context of environment/Dockerfile (`docker build -f environment/Dockerfile .`).
# That image is the agent's container and `COPY . /timeseriesgym` makes everything in the
# context readable by the agent, so only what the grading server needs is sent: the package
# and the environment files. Everything else in a checkout stays out: git history, the Git LFS
# archive of raw challenge data (timeseriesgym/data/, which holds test answers), earlier runs,
# prepared data, .env files and caches.
*
!environment/
!timeseriesgym/
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE

timeseriesgym/data/
# reference solution of the feature-enhancement challenge
timeseriesgym/competitions/*/example/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.env
